  "rationale": "Vervet (Chlorocebus sabaeus) genome-wide knockout library in Vero E6 cells (Grodzki et al. 2022). Column names match the GSM titles (T0puro = Day 0, Cov = SARS-CoV-2 infected, OC43-st = OC43 single-infected, OC43-nd = OC43 double-infected). Surviving cells were sequenced after infection; the authors ran MAGeCK on infected replicates vs the uninfected Day 0 library and read the positive (enriched) side. Infected and Day 0 replicates are separate cultures, so no replicate term. The library has no non-targeting guides, so calibration and the control null cannot be checked. Second analysis: OC43 initial infection vs Day 0 (Additional file 5). Selection is extreme (in one infected library the top 1% of guides hold 97% of reads), so library totals would call nearly every gene depleted; totals are median-ratio size factors and enrichment is read first.",
